NOTE: the supported package is built with nfpm from packaging/nfpm.yaml (package
name darkstat-nw). The Debian-style files in this directory (control, postinst,
rules) are legacy and are NOT used by that build. See packaging/README.md.

darkstat-nw packaging notes
===========================

Service configuration
---------------------

Edit /etc/default/darkstat-nw and set:

  INTERFACES="<linux-interface>"   (space-separated for several)

INTERFACES is auto-detected from the default route at install time when blank.
The package enables the service (systemctl enable) but does not start it.
Review the file, then start it:

  sudo systemctl start darkstat-nw

The default bind is loopback only (BINDADDR="127.0.0.1"); binding any
non-private address requires API_KEY. Default port is 1667.

JSON endpoint test
------------------

After traffic is flowing, verify JSON export:

  curl -s http://127.0.0.1:1667/json | jq .
